---
{
  title: "chebyshev_distance"
}
---
### NAME

    chebyshev_distance() - Calculates the Chebyshev distance between two
    points: the number of steps between them when a diagonal step costs the
    same as a straight one, like a king in chess. Points may have any number
    of axes, so 2D and 3D coordinates both work.

### SYNOPSIS

    int chebyshev_distance( int *a, int *b );

### DESCRIPTION

    Calculates the Chebyshev distance between two points: the number of
    steps between them when a diagonal step costs the same as a straight
    one, like a king in chess. Points may have any number of axes, so 2D and
    3D coordinates both work.

### PARAMETERS

    a  (int*)
       The first point's coordinates.

    b  (int*)
       The second point's coordinates, in the same axis order as `a`.

### RETURN VALUES

    (int) The largest absolute difference along any one axis.

### ERRORS

    If either point is not a non-empty array of integers. If the points have
    different numbers of axes.

### EXAMPLE

    {{di1}}chebyshev_distance(({ 0, 2, 3 }), ({ 0, 5, 1 })) // 3{{di0}}
